{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1211867-veiled-serpent-style-and-other-neat-synergies-from-wtfhw","id":1211867,"title":"Veiled Serpent Style; And other Neat Synergies from WTFHW","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-26T10:05:42-07:00","id":1211867,"title":"Veiled Serpent Style; And other Neat Synergies from WTFHW","content":"So initiatially I was kind of sad when I read White Veil because I apparently have the reading comprehension skills of a particularly bright horse or, perhaps, a particularly dim gorilla (but you know, one of those gorillas that paints and knows sign language. Sort of a \u2018bottom of the barrel of the cream of the crop\u2019 situation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it occurs to me\u2014 given their mutual facility with barehanded strikes and snakes capstone charm and reliance on Initiative and White Veil\u2019s entry level charm that the two harmonize really nicely. White veils Blithe Unruffled Plumage (which I think was supposed to Be Reflexive) provides a nice boost to soak which compliments snake style well\u2014 armor pericing fang could be useful for when you really need to burn your big initiative lead to kill someone now.<br /> <br /> White veil also gels really nicely with Black Claw (somewhat predictably), though I\u2019m not such a fan of the \u201cbeautiful rose, deadly thorns\u201d/femme fatale trope often applied to female characters (though certainly not exclusively) which the combination seems to encourage (not making a comment on authorial intent, just that it seems like the kind of character mechanically supported by those two used together). Also not condemning the trope itself, it\u2019s just not the kind of character that sings to me.<br /> <br /> Ebom shadow also is nice choice.<br /> <br /> Also looking at Golden Jannisary it seems like it would be a pretty useful and interesting martial art for a sorcerer\u2014 particularly one with the amulet-driven sorcerous initiation.<br /> <br /> What other neat combinations of martial arts (either inter style synergies or synergies with other effects) have people noticed and what sorts of characters have they inspire in your mind?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m talking mostly about stuff in WTFHW here but share anything you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:23:38-07:00","id":1212015,"title":"","content":"So, ones that jumped out to me are Golden Janissary+White Reaper + Zenith=the Zenithyst Zenith to ever Zenith.<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon+Stell Devil= ultimate Dragonblooded burning blades silliness<br /> <br /> Wood+Crane for interesting wrackstaff fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:06:30-07:00","id":1212089,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of Mantis + Black Claw. Poison someone, then grab them and restrain them forever until they die from the poison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:36:05-07:00","id":1212097,"title":"","content":"I wanna check how Golden Janissary plays into Righteous devil. Seems like a good fit in themes anyway.<br /> I've nicknamed Ebon Shadow and Tiger as Jaguar Style in my current games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:46:56-07:00","id":1212100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1211867-veiled-serpent-style-and-other-neat-synergies-from-wtfhw?p=1212097#post1212097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanna check how Golden Janissary plays into Righteous devil. Seems like a good fit in themes anyway.<br /> I've nicknamed Ebon Shadow and Tiger as Jaguar Style in my current games.</div> </div> </div> </div>They problem is that Golden Janissary while being thematically similar, is blocked from interacting meaningfully with RDS due to the latter being a flame-piece only MA, and GJ only working unarmed or spears. This makes them incompatible except as potential back ups rather than combination. Specifically on pg 426 &quot;Whenever a Martial Arts Charm refers to enhancing or creating an \u201cattack,\u201d it always means an attack made with one of that style\u2019s weapons.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:49:35-07:00","id":1212101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1211867-veiled-serpent-style-and-other-neat-synergies-from-wtfhw?p=1212100#post1212100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They problem is that Golden Janissary while being thematically similar, is blocked from interacting meaningfully with RDS due to the latter being a flame-piece only MA, and GJ only working unarmed or spears. This makes them incompatible except as potential back ups rather than combination. Specifically on pg 426 &quot;Whenever a Martial Arts Charm refers to enhancing or creating an \u201cattack,\u201d it always means an attack made with one of that style\u2019s weapons.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah!But, you forget. RDS form lets you treat the flamepiece as a staff or spear!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:54:36-07:00","id":1212102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1211867-veiled-serpent-style-and-other-neat-synergies-from-wtfhw?p=1212101#post1212101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah!But, you forget. RDS form lets you treat the flamepiece as a staff or spear!</div> </div> </div> </div>So I did, carry on! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: This does lock you to only RDS' form though, as form charms iirc are not cross compatible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:07:27-07:00","id":1212115,"title":"","content":"Tiger + Mantis is super deadly. The tiger style grappling charms are really good, and Leaping Mantis Technique is the best lead-in a tiger could want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:38:54-07:00","id":1212128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1211867-veiled-serpent-style-and-other-neat-synergies-from-wtfhw?p=1212102#post1212102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: This does lock you to only RDS' form though, as form charms iirc are not cross compatible</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe create a variant on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/892708-trying-to-choose-charms-for-a-gun-reaper-style-of-dawn-caste\">Burning Reaper Combination</a> that allows the martial artist to use a bayoneted firewand as a spear in Golden Janissary Form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:38:38-07:00","id":1212143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1211867-veiled-serpent-style-and-other-neat-synergies-from-wtfhw?p=1212128#post1212128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe create a variant on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/892708-trying-to-choose-charms-for-a-gun-reaper-style-of-dawn-caste\">Burning Reaper Combination</a> that allows the martial artist to use a bayoneted firewand as a spear in Golden Janissary Form?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's less neccessary. White Reaper relies on being in form for the majority of it's effects, in order to gain halos. Golden Janissary lacks that problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:29:47-07:00","id":1212220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1211867-veiled-serpent-style-and-other-neat-synergies-from-wtfhw?p=1212015#post1212015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, ones that jumped out to me are Golden Janissary+White Reaper + Zenith=the Zenithyst Zenith to ever Zenith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget to add Zelator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T13:40:22-07:00","id":1212410,"title":"","content":"Anyone seeing any synergies between Tiger and Water Dragon? Although they share a style weapon as always (and you can wear light armor in both), I'm not seeing any obvious nasty tricks here. I recall enjoying this combination in previous editions though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1211867-veiled-serpent-style-and-other-neat-synergies-from-wtfhw?p=1212143#post1212143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's less neccessary. White Reaper relies on being in form for the majority of it's effects, in order to gain halos. Golden Janissary lacks that problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite true, it's definitely nowhere near as crucial -- but if you'd rather use Golden Janissary Form sometimes without switching weapons (like if demons are attacking and you really want that +1 Parry), it could still be helpful. Probably would only need to be a one-dot Merit IMO, given the lack of halo issues.<br /> <br /> I just find the idea of mixing two styles but needing to stay in the Form of only one of them all the time to be awkward. It's more interesting when you have to decide which Form suits your situation best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:30:29-07:00","id":1213065,"title":"","content":"Was just thinking about what the Dragonblooded book meant for (Supernal and Non-Supernal) Martial Artists!<br /> <br /> Golden Janissary Style or &quot;CoD Genocide, the style&quot;<br /> The ability to knock people prone on withering attacks for 3m is amazing low hanging fruit for an entry charm. I could see anyone picking up that charm and being pleased with the result. <br /> <br /> I could see White Reaper, Tiger and/or Righteous Devil going up to the reflexive clash charm and the reflexive rush and attack when you incapacitate someone charm for a 5 to 6 charm investment. The last two charms absolutely melt (groups of) CoD into slag. Tiger style, at minimum, is going to want to get the charm that knocks people prone on hit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mantis Style or &quot;The Art of Giving Hugs&quot;<br /> A single charm dip lets you make Control Rolls using Dexterity, and it is mote efficient. This potentially opens up the tactic to people who might not have had it before. Mantis Form also has one of the better general purpose Martial Arts forms, without being reliant on it.<br /> <br /> Black Claw stylists will want to make the 4 charm investment that gives then a Restrain move (usable in Storm Calling Embrace) that persists their grapple (and thus, potentially, their poison) forever. Tiger Style has significant synergy with Mantis' rush-people-to-set-up-attacks charm. Either of those will benefit from taking another two charms to get a cheap clash-with-grapples charms.<br /> <br /> Someone who focuses on Mantis is going to be amazing one on one, when they can grapple. That said, I feel its a style that really needs another style to round it out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> White Veil - The Style that Isn't<br /> This is anprerty good style on its own. Black Claw gives it another poison to trigger and they have attrobute synergy. Ebon Shadow plays into the stealth themes, and combining their ambush charms is devestating. Snake is a good combination for reasons already stated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}